## Authoring checks that fit the existing scope

1. For every desk, identify the concrete work accomplished by its actual outputs; several intersecting branches are welcome. Do not force every thinker mentioned in the architecture to receive a token recipe.
2. Audit cross-time edges for both semantic contribution and historical/retrospective status. A source badge or a continuity count alone cannot prove either.
3. Look for consecutive recipes that merely rename their last input, add generic “criticism,” or finish with “report,” “understanding,” or “method.” Replace weak cases locally, not by inventing new mechanics.
4. Confirm that important alternatives survive in ordinary play, not only optional Read. A rival need not remain scientifically viable forever; distinguish a historically live rival from a continuing practical/philosophical alternative.
5. Judge the full candidate at its actual intended size and with normal highlighting. Static route success is not a human-enjoyment claim; neither is an AI stop a mandate to shorten the game.

